 "_hotspot_note": "Hotspot was transcribed with four merged pieces: two pairs of stacked buildings stored as single 18-cell blocks, and two pairs of adjacent 1x2 containers stored as single 4-cell blocks, which is not a legal piece. Split against the card art in assets/battlefield/hotspot.webp by overlaying a fitted 12x12 grid.",
 "_card_vs_art": "Where the Battlefield card legends disagree with their own printed maps, the maps win, because that is what you lay out. Crossroads: the map draws 6 containers 1x2, the legend lists 4. Hotspot: the map draws 4 low walls, the legend lists 6. Alley agrees with itself at 6/6/6/6/6.",
 "_card_note": "envCards is the Environment Card allowance printed on the Battlefield Card (rulebook 5.4.1); it is 4 on every 12x12 layout. legend is the terrain list as PRINTED, which _card_vs_art records disagreeing with the printed map in two places - the map wins there, because that is what you lay out. The en names are the ones printed on the cards; the IDS are the older names (alley, crossroads, hotspot) and are kept because saved boards carry them."
}
